    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d264">

                <pb facs="0372" n="292" sameAs="frus:frus1930v01/pg292"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.154/253: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Panama</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Davis</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-10-11T16:00:00-05:00">October 11, 1930—4
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>68. Your 69, October 10, 5 p.m. Honduras has requested cooperation. See mail
                    instruction 69 dated October 1<anchor n="12" xml:id="d264-f1"/> and enclosed
                    instruction same date to Chairman Forbes of Committee.</p>
                <p>On same date the Legation at Tegucigalpa was instructed also by mail to ascertain
                    and report so that the engineers might be informed whether it will be agreeable
                    to the Government of Honduras to have the survey begun within that country as
                    soon as or whenever this Government’s engineers may be able or find it
                    convenient to proceed to that country. No reply has yet been received. As soon
                    as it is, you will be informed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Castle</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
